<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43321" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐᾰγής</span></b>  (A), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ές</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄγος</span> A) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>free from pollution, pure</i>: </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b> of persons, <i>guiltless</i>,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ δὲ ἀποκτείνας τὸν ταῦτα ποιήσαντα
				. . ὅσιος ἔστω καὶ εὐ</span>. Lex ap.<i><span class="en">
				And.
				1.96
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Porph.
				<u>VP</u>
				15
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐαγεστάτων ἱππέων</span>, 
				v.l. for
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐγενεστάτων</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				10.13
			</span></i>; of bees, <i>chaste</i> (cf. Virg.<i><span class="en">
				<u>G.</u>
				4.198
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				9.404.7
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Antiphil.
			</span></i>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> of actions,
				<i>holy, lawful</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τίς οἶδεν εἰ
				κάτωθεν εὐαγῆ τάδε</span>; <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ant.</u>
				521
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐαγές ἐστι τὸ ἀποκτεῖναι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					9.44
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				538
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				App.
				<u>BC</u>
				2.148
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῦτο δ᾽ οὐκ εὐαγές μοι ἀπέβη</span>
			<i>wellomened, favourable</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Ep.</u>
				312a
			</span></i>. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐαγέως, ἔρδειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>h.Cer.</u>
					274
				</span></i>
			,<i><span class="en">
				369
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				2.699
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>POxy.</u>
				1203.5
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(i A.D.)</span>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐκ εὐαγῶς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ph.
					2.472
				</span></i>
			: 
				Sup.
			-<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">έστατα</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Jul.
				<u>Or.</u>
				7.230d
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> of offerings
			or services, <i>undefiled</i>: hence, <i>lawful</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐλέφας . . οὐκ εὐ. ἀνάθημα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Lg.</u>
					956a
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θυηλαί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					1.1140
				</span></i>
			, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕμνοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					7.34
				</span></i>
			 (Antip. Sid.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λύσις</span> a
			solution <i>free from defilement</i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OT</u>
				921
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐκ εὐ. ἀπολογίαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Porph.
					<u>Abst.</u>
					2.10
				</span></i>
			. (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Εὐηάγης</span> as pr. n., <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				12(9).56.118
			</span></i> (Styra, <span class="entity">v B.C.</span>).)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
